The PostgreSQL database driver is the `DB` struct in `store/db/postgres/postgres.go`. `NewDB` returns it as a `store.Driver`:

```16:39:store/db/postgres/postgres.go
type DB struct {
	db      *sql.DB
	profile *profile.Profile
}

func NewDB(profile *profile.Profile) (store.Driver, error) {
	// ...
	var driver store.Driver = &DB{
		db:      db,
		profile: profile,
	}

	// Return the DB struct
	return driver, nil
}
```

It is selected when the profile driver is `"postgres"` in `store/db/db.go`:

```23:24:store/db/db.go
	case "postgres":
		driver, err = postgres.NewDB(profile)
```

The `store.Driver` interface is defined in `store/driver.go`; `DB` implements it via methods in the `postgres` package (e.g. `GetDB`, `Close`, `IsInitialized` in `postgres.go`, plus CRUD methods in other files under `store/db/postgres/`).

